{{also|Steinn}}
==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|steinn||stone}}, from {{inh|is|gmq-pro|ᛊᛏᚨᛁᚾᚨᛉ}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*stainaz||stone}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|stone}}, {{cog|de|Stein}}, {{cog|nl|steen}}, {{cog|da|sten}}, {{cog|nb|sten}}, {{cog|nn|stein}}, {{cog|sv|sten}}, {{cog|fo|steinur}}, {{cog|fy|stien}}, {{cog|nds|Steen}}. Ultimately from {{der|is|ine-pro|*steyh₂-||something hard}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/steitn/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|eitn|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|m|steins|steinar}}

# [[stone]], [[rock]]
# [[stone]], [[pit]], [[pip]] {{gloss|the seed of certain [[fruit]]}}
# {{lb|is|medicine}} a [[calculus]], a [[stone]]

