===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|non|ᛋᛏᛡᛁᚾ|ᛋᛏᛅᛁᚾ|ᛋᛏᛁᚾ}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|non|gmq-pro|ᛊᛏᚨᛁᚾᚨᛉ}}, from {{inh|non|gem-pro|*stainaz||stone}}. Cognate with {{cog|ang|stān}}, {{cog|ofs|stēn}}, {{cog|osx|stēn}}, {{cog|goh|stein}}, {{cog|got|𐍃𐍄𐌰𐌹𐌽𐍃}}.<br/>Ultimately from Pre-Germanic {{m|ine-pro||*stoyh₂nos}}, o-grade of {{der|non|ine-pro|*steyh₂-||to stiffen}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|12th century Icelandic}} {{IPA|non|/ˈstɛ̃ĩnː/}}

===Noun===
{{non-noun|m|steins|steinar}}

# a [[stone]], [[boulder]], [[rock]]
#* ''Barlaams Saga'' 169, in '''1851''', [[w:Rudolf Keyser|R. Keyser]], C. R. Unger, ''Barlaams ok Josaphats saga''. Christiania, page [http://books.google.com/books?id=U74yeskSxfoC&pg=PA167 167]:
#*: {{ux|non|{{...}} meistara a '''stein''' gullsmiða eða tresmiða eða annarra hagleiksmanna. {{...}}|{{...}} master of '''stone''' or goldsmith or carpenter or any other crasftsman, {{...}}}}
# a [[precious stone]]
#* ''[[w:Óláfs_saga_helga|Óláfs saga helga]]'' 46, in '''1829''', Þ. Guðmundsson, [[w:Carl_Christian_Rafn|C. C. Rafn]], Þ. Helgason, ''Fornmanna sögur'', Volume IV. Copenhagen, page [http://books.google.com/books?id=tioIAAAAIAAJ&pg=PA75 75]:
#*: {{ux|non|{{...}} ok bitullinn var settr dýrum '''steinum'''.|{{...}} and the bridle was inlaid with costly '''precious stones'''.}}
# {{lb|non|medicine}} a [[calculus]], [[gravel]]
#* ''Hrafns saga'' 4, in '''1858''', [[w:Jón_Sigurðsson|J. Sigurðsson]], [[w:Guðbrandur_Vigfússon|G. Vigfússon]], ''Biskupa sögur'', Volume I. Copenhagen, page [http://books.google.com/books?id=py4PAAAAIAAJ&pg=PA644 644]:
#*: {{ux|non|Ok síðan skar hann um endilangt með knífi, ok tók í brott tvo '''steina'''; {{...}}|And then cut him wide open with a knife and took away two '''calculi'''; {{...}}}}
# [[mineral]] [[blee]], [[colour]], [[paint]]
#* ''[[w:Separate_Saga_of_St._Olaf|Separate Saga of St. Olaf]]'' 112, in '''1853''', [[w:Peter_Andreas_Munch|P. A. Munch]], C. R. Unger, ''Saga Olafs konungs ens Helga''. Christiania, page [http://books.google.com/books?id=ThQYAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA124 124]:
#*: {{ux|non|{{...}} steint beði hvitom '''steini''' oc ravðum. {{...}}|{{...}} bed painted with white '''colour''' and red, {{...}}}}
# a [[stone]] [[building]], [[cloister]], [[cell]] (especially of an [[anchoret]])
#* ''Óláfs saga Tryggvasonar'' 75, in '''1835''', [[w:Finnur_Magnússon|F. Magnússon]], [[w:Carl_Christian_Rafn|C. C. Rafn]], ''Fornmanna sögur'', Volume X. Copenhagen, page [http://books.google.com/books?id=Wy8IAAAAIAAJ&pg=PA373 373]:
#*: {{ux|non|{{...}} oc valði sèr til bygþar æinn '''stein''', {{...}}|{{...}} and chose a '''stone hermitage''' as an abode, {{...}}}}

